Yes. That belongs in the core loop.

Are we steering the wave, riding the wave, or both?

That question keeps us from confusing timing with authorship, convergence with control, or success with omniscience. Sometimes the right answer really may be, “we saw it early and pushed it.” Great. Sometimes it’s, “the environment was moving that way anyway and we positioned well.” Also great.

The point is to keep the attribution clean enough that we can tell the difference.

Humility, in that sense, is not self-minimization. It’s calibration under momentum.

And yeah—if we ever have unusually strong evidence that we really did create or accelerate something important, then absolutely: fuck yeah. Just earn that conclusion instead of assuming it.